body:
I'm sorry the details on this are light, but basically everything worked in 4.0.19.Final. After updating to 20 I get inconsistent values when getting/reading from buffers. I've gone so far as to print the buffer's reader index and contents and then watching as it reads a value that isn't consistent with what was just printed.

The scary part is if I turn unsafe off (-Dio.netty.tryUnsafe=false) everything works fine again.

Hints:
Happens with pooled and unpooled buffers.
All my buffers are immediately changed ByteOrder.LITTLE_ENDIAN in handlers.
Mac OS X 10.9.3
JDK 8u5

Excerpt from a handler's decoding logic:

``` java
    @Override
    protected void decode(ChannelHandlerContext ctx, ByteBuf buffer, List<Object> out) throws Exception {
        buffer = buffer.order(ByteOrder.LITTLE_ENDIAN);

        while (buffer.readableBytes() >= HeaderLength &&
                buffer.readableBytes() >= getMessageLength(buffer)) {

            int messageLength = getMessageLength(buffer);
            MessageType messageType = MessageType.fromMediumInt(buffer.getMedium(buffer.readerIndex()));

            switch (messageType) {
                case SecureMessage:
                    onSecureMessage(ctx, buffer.readSlice(messageLength), out);
                    break;

                case Error:
                    onError(ctx, buffer.readSlice(messageLength));
                    break;

                default:
                    out.add(buffer.readSlice(messageLength).retain());
            }
        }
    }
```

getMessageLength() (HeaderLengthIndex = 4):

``` java
    default int getMessageLength(ByteBuf buffer) {
        System.out.println("getMessageLength() readerIndex=" + buffer.readerIndex() + " buffer=" + ByteBufUtil.hexDump(buffer));
        return Ints.checkedCast(buffer.getUnsignedInt(buffer.readerIndex() + HeaderLengthIndex));
    }
```

Logs, right before the exception:
getMessageLength() readerIndex=0 buffer=4d534746dd23000001000000010000000200000002000000 (truncated)

The stack trace:

```
io.netty.handler.codec.DecoderException: java.lang.IllegalArgumentException: Out of range: 4026531840
